<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  The kernel description package_xo is given, and the only place the platform
  is told what this kernel's ports are.

  The schema is the RTL Kernel Wizard's, taken from the example Vitis 2022.2
  ships rather than from memory:

    Vitis/2022.2/cli/examples/xo_kernel_srcs/rtl_kernel_wizard_0.xo
      rtl_kernel_wizard_0/kernel.xml

  and so is the range/dataWidth pairing: its s_axi_control is
  range="0x1000" dataWidth="32" with a twelve-bit address in the RTL, which is
  the aperture rtl/fpga/tnca_axi_lite.v was written with (S_AXI_ADDR_W = 12)
  and four times what the 0x00..0xA4 register map needs. The spare address
  space is not used and is not reserved for anything.

  WHAT IS NOT HERE, AND WHY

  ap_clk and ap_rst_n have no <port> entry. ap_clk is a system port the
  platform supplies and connects by name -- the wizard's kernel.xml does not
  list it either, and its constraints file is one line,
  `create_clock -period 4.000 [get_ports ap_clk]`. ap_rst_n is absent for a
  different reason: this kernel does not have one. rtl/board/tnca_u50_xo.v
  generates its reset from a counter off ap_clk, and the wizard's own top,
  which also has no ap_rst_n port, instantiates its control slave with
  `.ap_rst_n(1'b1)` -- so no external reset is taken to exist.

  <args/> is empty and is not decoration. This kernel has no scalar arguments:
  everything the host says to it is a register write, and everything it says
  back is a register read. hwControlProtocol is ap_ctrl_none for the same
  reason there is no ap_start -- the mailbox in rtl/fpga/tnca_mmio.v is the
  control protocol, and a second one generated alongside it would be a second
  thing claiming to own the device.

  interrupt is false. There is no interrupt port and no interrupt source. The
  host polls R_DOORBELL, which is what the transport already does when it
  reads a response file, so nothing is waiting for an edge that never comes.
-->
<root versionMajor="1" versionMinor="6">
  <kernel name="tnca_u50" language="ip_c" vlnv="tnca.com:kernel:tnca_u50:1.0"
          attributes="" preferredWorkGroupSizeMultiple="0" workGroupSize="1"
          interrupt="false" hwControlProtocol="ap_ctrl_none">
    <ports>
      <port name="s_axi_tnca" mode="slave" range="0x1000" dataWidth="32"
            portType="addressable" base="0x0"/>
    </ports>
    <args/>
  </kernel>
</root>
